1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Asta visits the village of Neon, home to Rebecca and her younger siblings.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Coincidentally, Gosha's beloved little sister Marie lives there as well.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Kay, come on and...

7
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Get away from her right now, you scum!

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
That night, a strange tragedy befell Neon.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
It's time... for you... to die.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
We don't even live here!

11
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
What? There's snow everywhere. Where'd it all come from? It's not even winter yet.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Hey! Stop it! What are you doing out here?

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,000
It's the children! They're missing!

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
No.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:23,000
How exciting. I just love making new friends.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
What is this?

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Ha

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:57,980
Thank you.

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:27,980
Thank you.

20
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:57,980
Thank you.

21
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:59,580
Why would they run off at this hour?

22
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:02,580
Possies!

23
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,660
Roland! Where are you?

24
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:06,280
Not playing hide-and-seek, I'm guessing.

25
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,200
Die, scum.

26
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:11,720
I will never allow you to marry my sister.

27
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,080
Come on, Ghosh! This is so not the time!

28
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:16,940
There is nothing in this world more important than my marine.

29
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:17,620
Nothing.

30
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:24,020
Can someone please tell me what's wrong with this village?

31
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,760
They need snow at this time of year? That is just absurd.

32
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:31,160
Hey, Noelle. What are you doing in neon?

33
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:35,160
Uh, just passing through, seeing the sights, that sort of thing, you know.

34
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,180
Asta, who is this?

35
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,160
A friend from the Magic Knights!

36
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,820
Noelle, this is my friend Rebecca.

37
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:43,580
His friend? His friend?

38
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:44,900
Uh...

39
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:45,920
What's wrong?

40
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:47,040
Oh, it's nothing.

41
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,840
Hey, listen.

42
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:54,140
A little while ago, I saw a bunch of kids headed toward the mountains.

43
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:55,300
What was that about?

44
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,960
Was there some kind of late-night festival?

45
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,120
The kids!

46
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:02,360
I have a festival of blood plant.

47
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:04,360
Stop that!

48
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,600
The hag!

49
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:07,560
Sister Granny!

50
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:10,300
The snow isn't natural.

51
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,800
I can sense some kind of spell in it.

52
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,880
One that controls people.

53
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:18,740
But only children whose magic has not yet developed.

54
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:22,380
Several of ours have disappeared as well.

55
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:25,880
Why would someone be spiriting all of these children away?

56
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,160
Wait, Crone.

57
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:28,820
You lost some of yours?

58
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:31,100
Marie better not have been one of them.

59
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,140
Unfortunately, she was.

60
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,320
Damn you!

61
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:37,980
You decrepit old fool!

62
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,620
How could you let this happen to her?

63
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:40,740
Stop! Please!

64
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:42,920
So quick to resort to violence!

65
00:04:43,420 --> 00:04:44,740
You truly are hopeless!

66
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:47,060
You can hit me if you want to,

67
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,840
but that's not going to bring them back!

68
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,380
It won't help Marie!

69
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,660
No, it won't.

70
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:57,760
But it will make me feel a hell of a lot better!

71
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,520
Get off of him!

72
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,780
What do you think you're doing?

73
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,260
Asta, you will die.

74
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:07,600
Hey now, why don't we stop for a second

75
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,780
to take a deep breath and cool off a little bit!

76
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:16,040
We're magic knights, after all.

77
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:18,560
We have to learn to remain calm.

78
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:19,460
You got it?

79
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:20,760
Well done.

80
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,380
I like this boy.

81
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:24,940
Calm, huh?

82
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:26,220
All right then.

83
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:27,540
I knew you'd come around.

84
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,240
I'll kill you very calmly.

85
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,160
That's not what I meant!

86
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:33,260
That's right, Brad.

87
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:34,540
I'm gonna make it hurt.

88
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:36,180
No, please stop!

89
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,420
We're wasting time!

90
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,460
We have to start looking for clues!

91
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:40,460
Oh yeah.

92
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:42,100
Like it's gonna be that easy.

93
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:43,280
Hmm.

94
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:47,480
I told Marie to keep her magic mirror with her at all times.

95
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:50,440
The snow will interfere with transmission magic.

96
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,840
But if we track down the mana in the mirror...

97
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,180
then we should be able to find her.

98
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,320
There, you see?

99
00:05:58,060 --> 00:05:59,180
Fine, you were right!

100
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,760
But don't think for a second

101
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,540
that's gonna keep me from stomping the life out of you maggot!

102
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:05,840
I'll come too.

103
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,760
The church's children are my responsibility.

104
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:10,960
Thanks, sister.

105
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,840
But maybe you should just let us handle it.

106
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:15,460
No, the hag is infuriating, but she does have her uses.

107
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:16,360
Really?

108
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:19,100
But isn't she kind of... old?

109
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:22,600
I can still teach you youngsters a thing or two.

110
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:23,880
Lasta?

111
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,760
Between Marco's immaturity and Luca's stubborn streak,

112
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:29,280
I'm really worried about them.

113
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:30,860
What am I going to do?

114
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,140
If anything happens to those two...

115
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:34,120
Hey, get it together!

116
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,200
You hear me?

117
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:40,260
I promise you, I'll bring your brother and sister back.

118
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:43,840
No moping, okay?

119
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:45,460
I don't think they would want that.

120
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:48,880
Yeah, you're right.

121
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:52,860
Let's go now.

122
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,540
You're not going to leave me behind, are you?

123
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:57,680
You can't fly on your own either.

124
00:06:58,160 --> 00:06:59,580
You want to be a dangler like him?

125
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:00,800
Hmm.

126
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:04,760
There's always a chance the village may be attacked again while we're gone.

127
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:06,920
Please stay here and look after it for me.

128
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:10,600
Oh, and let the magic knights know what's up!

129
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:13,240
Asta, we're counting on you!

130
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:13,640
Right.

131
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:15,040
I'm stuck here with her.

132
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:28,420
Oh, wow.

133
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:33,720
I can't believe how many new friends I've made.

134
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,780
Now, let's play nice, okay?

135
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:51,480
Where am I?

136
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,120
This isn't the church.

137
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:55,000
How did I get here?

138
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:59,080
And why does everyone look so strange?

139
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,240
So sweet.

140
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:01,120
Who is that man?

141
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:03,560
Good little children now, thanks to my magic.

142
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:05,940
Did he cast a spell on everyone?

143
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:07,280
Then why?

144
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:08,640
Oh, right.

145
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:10,360
The mirror my brother gave me.

146
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:13,080
He said it would protect me from magic a little bit.

147
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:16,560
Think of it as your big brother when I'm not there.

148
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:18,300
That's why I'm awake.

149
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:21,820
Oh, dear.

150
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,820
My spell's worn off this one.

151
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,280
Why is that?

152
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:27,220
It's too bad, really.

153
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:31,360
If I can't use my magic to make you a good girl, we can't be friends.

154
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:33,400
You want to be my friend, right?

155
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,980
No, not that way.

156
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:38,120
You shouldn't use spells to make people do what you want.

157
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,980
If you do that, you're not a real friend at all.

158
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:45,340
You don't belong here, you horrible little monster.

159
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:48,880
No friend of mine would ever say something like that.

160
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:54,180
Now, now.

161
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:56,100
Don't lose your temper, Mish.

162
00:08:56,820 --> 00:08:58,860
We don't want to damage the merchandise.

163
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:01,840
Do I have to do all your thinking for you?

164
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:02,980
No, please.

165
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:03,700
I'm sorry.

166
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:09,580
This one's our star.

167
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,200
A lot of power for a kid.

168
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:17,900
Any more like her, we'll be Richmond by the time we're done.

169
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:21,500
That kid hardly has any magic.

170
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:26,860
I told you to get the ones who were loaded, and this is what you bring me, really?

171
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:28,740
I'm sorry, Boro.

172
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:31,400
We don't need this trash.

173
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:32,440
Bye, kid!

174
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:44,580
Brother or not, keep wasting my time and I'll kill you.

175
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:50,260
Now then, time to start extracting some magic.

176
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,320
She's nearby.

177
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,560
The mana feels stronger here.

178
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:03,040
Okay!

179
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,780
Whoever's behind this has a good deal of power.

180
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:08,720
We have to keep our guards up.

181
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,220
Please, Marie.

182
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,000
Hold on.

183
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:12,340
We're coming, kids.

184
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:13,460
Hang in there.

185
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:26,460
Now, everyone, please stay calm.

186
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,760
The Magic Knights will find your children and bring them home safely.

187
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:30,440
Whoa!

188
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,840
Get a look at a rope.

189
00:10:32,380 --> 00:10:34,860
Are they really going to bring my son back to me?

190
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:36,360
Where are Marco and Luca?

191
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,100
What's going on?

192
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,180
I'm sorry, Pim.

193
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:40,580
It's all right.

194
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,340
Asta will bring them back.

195
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:43,280
I promise you.

196
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:45,700
Yes, they'll be home before you know it.

197
00:10:46,120 --> 00:10:46,460
Okay.

198
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,960
But what happened to our house?

199
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:53,200
Yeah, that's another thing silly Asta will be taking care of.

200
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:56,000
For now, let's just patch it up the best we can, okay?

201
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:58,260
It's gonna be freezing in there.

202
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:00,240
Right.

203
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:01,980
I need to contact the other knights.

204
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:09,020
Hello there, Knights Headquarters here.

205
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:11,620
Hey, I recognize you.

206
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:13,820
They have you working at headquarters?

207
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:14,660
Ha ha!

208
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:20,740
Captain Jack stationed me here to help out temporarily, but I'm not gonna be a full-time paper pusher or anything.

209
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:27,220
I've just accomplished so much in my short time with the praying mantises that I've earned myself a little break from battle, you see?

210
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:27,660
Ha ha!

211
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:30,120
We've got an emergency here, you babbling idiot!

212
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,840
Listen, there's snow falling in neon!

213
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:33,600
Really?

214
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:34,920
How romantic.

215
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,900
Do you understand the word emergency?

216
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:41,120
Somebody used magic to make it snow so they can abduct children from the village!

217
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,140
Wait, huh?

218
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,820
You should tell the magic knights right away!

219
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,280
What do you think I'm doing now?

220
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:49,060
Right, well, don't worry.

221
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,440
Seke is on the case.

222
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,060
Ha ha!

223
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:55,480
I don't find that reassuring, idiot.

224
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,840
I'm picking up mana over there.

225
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,120
Yes, that's it!

226
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:10,580
The caves would be a perfect place to keep all of the children hidden.

227
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:12,240
Marco!

228
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:14,680
Hang on, Ghosh!

229
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,680
Can you set me down over there for a sec?

230
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,280
Leave him.

231
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:19,440
My angel's the only one who matters.

232
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:22,120
If you want off, then let go.

233
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:22,680
Ha ha!

234
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:31,200
Asta!

235
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:33,520
And you're a magic knight!

236
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,200
Don't they have standards anymore?

237
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:41,060
I couldn't care less what happens to anybody else.

238
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:43,000
As long as Marie stays safe.

239
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:49,960
Just like the captain told me the day I cast aside my prisoner's clothing and joined the Black Bulls.

240
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,420
I won't stop you.

241
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,360
Go on and protect whatever you think needs protecting.

242
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:58,180
And that's just what I'm gonna do.

243
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:00,320
Marco!

244
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,180
Stay with us.

245
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:03,620
The poor thing.

246
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:06,260
He's covered in scrapes and frostbitten, too.

247
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:07,140
Marco!

248
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:08,520
Can you hear me?

249
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,780
It's no use.

250
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:12,380
He's in some kind of trance.

251
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,840
All right.

252
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,860
Just leave it to me!

253
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:17,920
Wait!

254
00:13:18,080 --> 00:13:19,060
What are you going to do?

255
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:25,480
Hold on.

256
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:26,100
What?

257
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:27,780
Asta...

258
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:28,420
Sister?

259
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:29,960
Hey, kid.

260
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:30,700
How are you feeling?

261
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:34,020
He dispelled the magic with the touch of his sword.

262
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,420
It hurts so much!

263
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,120
Hold on.

264
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,200
Flame healing magic.

265
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,340
Sacred healing light.

266
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:45,880
Thank you.

267
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,640
I'm a lot warmer now.

268
00:13:48,380 --> 00:13:49,700
That's amazing, Granny.

269
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:51,540
You can use healing magic?

270
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:53,260
Tell us, child.

271
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:54,320
What happened?

272
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:55,120
I'm sorry.

273
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,620
I don't really know.

274
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:59,520
Someone sure roughed him up.

275
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:00,560
Marco!

276
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:04,200
